laura:Rotation a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "Euler-angle rotation relative to the global coordinate system. All angles are in radians, bounded to [-pi, pi]. The composition is Rz(psi) . Rx(phi) . Ry(theta), as implemented by laura.utils.rotation_matrix.euler_angles_to_rotation_matrix; each angle below names the axis that factor turns about. psi and theta were described the other way round until 2026-09-01, which is how the Bmad importer came to read x_pitch (a rotation about y) into psi." ;
